$ Shallow-water propagation over a submerged bar with LTA triads, with the
$ third-harmonic term as TU Delft 41.51 computes it
$
$ The same deck as triad_lta.swn, with one word more on the TRIAD line:
$ UPSTREAM. Since 41.51 the LTA (ITRIAD = 1) lets waves at f and 2f feed the
$ third harmonic at 3f. Upstream takes the energy for that only from f, as
$ twice the density gained at 3f, and nothing from 2f, so one third of what
$ arrives at 3f is not taken from anywhere. The fork shares the loss as the
$ triad requires, one third from f and two thirds from 2f (BF-63); this deck
$ asks for the upstream form instead, and is what upstream computes for
$ triad_lta.swn.
$
$ UPSTREAM is a keyword of this fork, not upstream input, and only valid with
$ the LTA. It must be the last word on the TRIAD line.
PROJECT 'TRIADLTU' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30.0 0.0 300 0 &
      SECTOR -10.0 10.0 20 0.10 2.0 31
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30 0 1.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.06 2.0 0.0 2.0

GEN3 WESTH
OFF WINDGROWTH
OFF WCAPPING
OFF QUADRUPLET
TRIAD LTA UPSTREAM

POINTS 'GAUGES' 2.0 0.0 10.0 0.0 15.0 0.0 18.0 0.0 &
         25.0 0.0 30.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'triad_lta_upstream.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'triad_lta_upstream.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 15.0 0.0 S1D 'triad_lta_upstream_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
